---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const asideLinks = [
  { label: 'Using the site', href: '#using-the-site' },
  { label: 'No professional advice', href: '#no-professional-advice' },
  { label: 'Acceptable use', href: '#acceptable-use' },
  { label: 'Third-party links', href: '#third-party-links' },
  { label: 'Intellectual property', href: '#intellectual-property' },
  { label: 'Disclaimers and liability', href: '#disclaimers-and-liability' },
  { label: 'Changes', href: '#changes' },
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Terms and conditions"
  metaTitle="Terms and Conditions for Using FixProblemNow"
  description="The terms that apply when you use FixProblemNow: informational purpose, acceptable use, third-party links, intellectual property and liability."
  canonical="/terms/"
  eyebrow="Terms"
  intro="These terms apply when you access or use FixProblemNow. By using the site, you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site."
  updated="2026-11-15"
  asideLinks={asideLinks}
  asideNote="Nothing in these terms limits rights that cannot be excluded under applicable law."
>
  <h2 id="using-the-site">Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    FixProblemNow provides general troubleshooting information for personal and internal business
    use. You may read, print, and share links to the content. You may not present the content as
    your own, republish it at scale, or use it to train a commercial product without written
    permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is provided on an “as available” basis. Access may be interrupted for maintenance,
    security, or reasons outside the operator’s control. No account, subscription, or service-level
    commitment is offered.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-professional-advice">No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    The content is general information, not professional advice. It is not a substitute for
    diagnosis by a qualified technician, legal advice, financial advice, medical advice, or the
    official instructions supplied with a device. You are responsible for deciding whether a step is
    appropriate for your equipment, your data, and your level of experience.
  </p>
  <p>
    Always read the safety notes and the “when to stop” section of a guide. If a device is smoking,
    sparking, unusually hot, or has a swollen battery, stop and seek qualified help.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the site to break the law or infringe another person’s rights.</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the server, other users, or connected systems.</li>
    <li>Submit malicious code, spam, or automated requests that disrupt the service.</li>
    <li>Use the contact form to send passwords, recovery keys, or other sensitive credentials.</li>
    <li>Misrepresent an affiliation with FixProblemNow or a manufacturer.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Access may be limited or blocked if these rules are broken or if a request pattern threatens the
    availability or security of the site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party-links">Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Guides link to manufacturer support pages, operating-system documentation, and other third-party
    sites. Those sites have their own terms and privacy policies. A link is not an endorsement of
    everything on the destination site, and the destination may change after the guide is published.
    Verify that a download comes from the manufacturer’s official domain before installing it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="intellectual-property">Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The original text, site design, and branding on FixProblemNow are protected by applicable
    intellectual-property law. Manufacturer names, product names, and logos remain the property of
    their respective owners and are used for identification and compatibility only. Nothing on the
    site grants a licence to use another party’s trademark.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimers-and-liability">Disclaimers and liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, the site is provided without warranties of any kind,
    express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. The
    operator does not warrant that a guide is complete, current, or suitable for your specific device
    or situation.
  </p>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, the operator is not liable for indirect, incidental,
    special, consequential, or punitive losses, or for loss of data, profits, revenue, or business
    opportunity, arising from use of or reliance on the site. Nothing in these terms excludes or
    limits liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, including liability for death or
    personal injury caused by negligence where such limitation is prohibited.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated when the site changes. The date at the top of the page shows the last
    update. Continued use after a change means the updated terms apply. If a provision is found
    unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue in effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. See
    also the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> and
    <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
